00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.670 align:start position:0%
finally leaders of germany's main  parties have agreed on a coalition pact  the deal ends two months of wrangling  spd leader sigma gabriel  chancellor angela merkel and christian  social union leader host zhoufer  were all smiles at a signing ceremony  and this is what the deal looks like a  manifesto for germany's future  after that leaders left the ceremony for  a press conference  there angela merkel outlined her new  government's priorities  for this accord is in the spirit of a  grand coalition  we're aiming to solve germany's big  challenges  i think that those challenges can be  grouped into three categories  one solid finances two assuring  prosperity and three  social security  the deal is done but spd leader sigma  gabriel now has to secure a yes vote  from his party's rank and file  many are opposed so gabriel is trying to  allay concerns  a lot of places this coalition deal  proves that politics isn't a lofty  pursuit  something that's decided in parliament  or the chancellor's office politics is  about people's lives  about their concerns hopes and  opportunities  the leaders agreed on a deal early on  wednesday morning  many germans wonder why it took them so  long to agree  if the majority in germany thinks we  should have a grand coalition  then it could have all gone a bit faster  it's about time that we got an effective  government again  it took long enough i think in the long  run a grant coalition is not going to be  good for one of the two partners  in this case the spd that is if the spd  rank and file agree to the deal  the results of a party ballot are  expected mid-december  if they approve germany will get its  third-ever grand coalition government
 

